    {
      "file": "src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c",
      "function": "opj_j2k_read_tlm",
      "line": 3767,
      "code": "l_tile_part_infos[l_tlm->m_entries_count].m_tile_index =\n    (OPJ_UINT16)l_tile_index;\nl_tile_part_infos[l_tlm->m_entries_count].m_length = l_length;\n++l_tlm->m_entries_count;",
      "note": "First project statement that materializes the attacker-controlled TLM tile-part table used by the vulnerable path. The staged PoC contains one TLM entry for tile 0, so decoder state records exactly one tile-part description before the later SOT mismatch is processed.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c",
      "function": "opj_j2k_read_sod",
      "line": null,
      "code": "l_cstr_index->tile_index[p_j2k->m_current_tile_number].tp_index[l_current_tile_part].end_header\n    =\n        l_current_pos;",
      "note": "The vulnerable code dereferences `tp_index[l_current_tile_part]` without checking that `tp_index` is non-null and that `l_current_tile_part < nb_tps`. The fix adds exactly that guard before the `end_header` and `end_pos` stores.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c",
      "function": "opj_j2k_read_sod",
      "line": 5085,
      "code": "l_cstr_index->tile_index[p_j2k->m_current_tile_number].tp_index[l_current_tile_part].end_header\n    =\n        l_current_pos;",
      "note": "The vulnerable code dereferences `tp_index[l_current_tile_part]` without checking that `tp_index` is non-null and that `l_current_tile_part < nb_tps`. The fix adds exactly that guard before the `end_header` and `end_pos` stores.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c",
      "function": "opj_j2k_read_sod",
      "line": null,
      "code": "l_cstr_index->tile_index[p_j2k->m_current_tile_number].tp_index[l_current_tile_part].end_header\n    =\n        l_current_pos;",
      "note": "ASAN crash site. `l_current_tile_part` is 1 while tile 0's `tp_index` heap buffer has only one element, so storing `end_header` through `tp_index[1]` writes eight bytes past the 24-byte allocation.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
